css34: SourcePawn 2: forwards into variadic or short-handed callbacks crash

Runtime::InvokeMethod (forwards, Call_Finish, any IPluginFunction call into a
plugin compiled by the 1.13 spcomp) reserved and filled only the arguments the
caller passed. The callee's frame has one slot per signature entry, and a
legacy variadic function (`f(a, b, ...)`) takes its extra arguments as a
packed array ([count, values...]) in its last slot. The invoker drops
trailing arguments a callback does not declare, so a variadic callback got
fewer cells than its frame: the pack slot held stale stack data, and the
callee's registers ran one cell past the reserved stack, where the next
native call wrote its parameters. testsuite fwdtest1 (a private forward into
`ZohMyGod(num, const String:format[], ...)`) segfaulted srcds that way.

InvokeMethod now reserves every signature slot, zero-fills formal arguments
the caller left out, and passes a pack of the remaining arguments (count 0
when there are none) to a variadic callee, the same layout the lowering builds
for script-to-script calls. Upstream sourcepawn at our pin has the same code.

diff --git a/vm/v2/runtime.cpp b/vm/v2/runtime.cpp
index dc5efb20f7a9ea22e9657dc403e0a778ffe389a7..06476d2f82e6721335c0fd28f37cb651e50a982f 100644
--- a/vm/v2/runtime.cpp
+++ b/vm/v2/runtime.cpp
@@ -699,13 +699,39 @@ bool Runtime::InvokeMethod(uint32_t method_index, const cell_t* params,
 
     ke::SaveRestore<uint32_t> save_sp(env_->sp());
 
+    // The callee reads one argument slot per entry of its signature; a
+    // legacy variadic function takes its extra arguments as one packed array
+    // ([count, values...]) in its last slot. Callers such as forwards pass a
+    // flat list instead, so build that layout here: missing formal arguments
+    // become 0 and anything beyond them goes into the pack. Without this the
+    // pack slot was left as whatever was on the stack, and the first
+    // variadic use (e.g. VFormat) dereferenced it.
+    uint32_t arg_slots = (uint32_t)method->signature()->args().size();
+    bool variadic = method->IsLegacyVariadic();
+    uint32_t formal_argc = variadic ? arg_slots - 1 : arg_slots;
+
+    uint32_t pack_addr = 0;
+    if (variadic) {
+        uint32_t extra = num_params > formal_argc ? num_params - formal_argc : 0;
+        pack_addr = env_->sp();
+        if (!env_->addStack((extra + 1) * sizeof(cell_t)))
+            return false;
+        cell_t* pack = env_->heap().ToPhysAddr<cell_t*>(pack_addr);
+        pack[0] = (cell_t)extra;
+        for (uint32_t i = 0; i < extra; i++)
+            pack[i + 1] = params[formal_argc + i];
+    }
+
     uint32_t frame_base = env_->sp();
-    if (!env_->addStack(num_params * sizeof(cell_t)))
+    uint32_t frame_slots = arg_slots > num_params ? arg_slots : num_params;
+    if (!env_->addStack(frame_slots * sizeof(cell_t)))
         return false;
     cell_t* sp = env_->heap().ToPhysAddr<cell_t*>(frame_base);
 
-    for (unsigned int i = 0; i < num_params; i++)
-        sp[i] = params[i];
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < formal_argc; i++)
+        sp[i] = i < num_params ? params[i] : 0;
+    if (variadic)
+        sp[formal_argc] = (cell_t)pack_addr;
 
     // Enter the execution engine.
     bool ok = env_->Invoke(this, method->GetFunction(), frame_base, result);
